  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a 2D grid of characters, where the position in the grid is filled if its a '#', else it would be a '.' . With the filled cells the grid can form a structure which can represent a '1' or a '0'. \n\nExample: The following figure represents a '1', cause it doesn't encircle a void.\n\n......\n\n...#...\n\n...#...\n\n...#...\n\n...#...\n\n\n\nThe following figure on the other hand, represents a '0', cause it encircles a void.\n\n..........\n\n..........\n\n..#####...\n\n..#...#...\n\n..#...#...\n\n..#####...\n\n..........\n\n\n\nPrint 1 if the '#'s structure forms a '1' else print 0 in case it forms a '0'. \n\nDiagonal entry into the void is not allowed.\n\nIt is guaranteed that in the grid there would be only one '1' or one '0' represented.\n\nCheck examples for clarity, and all quotes are for clarity.\n\n\n\n\n\nInput Format\nInput will start with 2 integers **x** and **y** separated by a single space, on a newline. **x** lines of strings of length **y** each would follow, representing the 2D grid. Each character in the grid would either be a '#' or a '.'.\n\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint 0 or 1, depending on the input.",
    "constraints": [
      "4&lt;=x,y&lt;=50"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "7 10\n..........\n....#.....\n....#.....\n....#.....\n....#.....\n....#.....\n..........",
        "output": "1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere is no void by the structure formed, so its a 1."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "7 10\n.####.....\n.#..#.....\n.#..#.....\n.#..#.....\n.#..#.....\n..###.....\n..........",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nSince, there is void inside the '#' structure, so its a 0. Note, diagonal movement is not allowed."
      }
    ]
  },
